-## 3.2. Data Node
+## 3.2. Data Node
 
 A Data Node represents one cartographic feature.
 
 Binary unpacking format:
 
 ```text
-<iiiiIII
+<iiiiBII
````

| Offset        | Size          | Type       | Description                     |                                               |
| :------------ | :------------ | :--------- | :------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |
| `0x00 - 0x0F` | 16            | `int32[4]` | BBox `[xmin, ymin, xmax, ymax]` |                                               |
| -             | `0x10 - 0x13` | 4          | `uint32`                        | **Type** — PurrGO feature code                |
| -             | `0x14 - 0x17` | 4          | `uint32`                        | **v1** — pointer to geometry record in `.mlp` |
| -             | `0x18 - 0x1B` | 4          | `uint32`                        | **v2** — record index in `.db`                |
| +             | `0x10`        | 1          | `uint8`                         | **Type** — PurrGO feature code                |
| +             | `0x11 - 0x14` | 4          | `uint32`                        | **v1** — pointer to geometry record in `.mlp` |
| +             | `0x15 - 0x18` | 4          | `uint32`                        | **v2** — record index in `.db`                |

*

+The feature code is stored as a single unsigned byte.
+
+`text
+0 = NO_CLASS
+`
+
+The remaining feature-code values are defined by `features.csv`.
